  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "text": "Ongoing issue for some time now. It fails to recognise pets in a lot of photos. If I type in search bar \"dogs\", those pet photos appear, however if I just go through People and Pets, photos do not appear despite turning on the pets function. It recognises some but not others.. edit: face groups was turned on and still not working..",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "069518e9-1250-41a0-bc6b-5a550e521b4a",
      "date": "2026-08-31",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "face_recognition_misidentification"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    },
    {
      "text": "It's limited but so effective! The other day a friend asked for photos of her sister (also a friend) that I had because it's her birthday and she wanted to make a collage. I just searched on Google Photos by her name and it found a bunch because of the face classification. That's some good shit.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "source_id": "hn_23521809",
      "date": "2020-06-14",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "face_recognition_misidentification"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "Google photos is tracking my face and anyone else whose photos I have taken from my phone and I cannot turn this off. They enable a \"search photos by people\" feature. I find this creepy and ominous. I never asked for this. Can I sue them for them to stop?",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "source_id": "hn_20653457",
      "date": "2019-08-09",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "face_recognition_misidentification"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "keep getting a pop up and can't get rid of it. it tells me Google arranges photos by face recognition.",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "1b970912-a0bd-4375-a646-bfb3ab481c21",
      "date": "2026-08-16",
      "confidence": 0.85,
